&Q000460

{1 = 1-8}
1.	Lady, going to the sweet-voiced cows and gentle-voiced calves in the cattle-pen, young woman, when you arrive there, @wDN{Inana}, may the churn sound! May the churn of your spouse sound, @wDN{Inana}, may the churn sound! May the churn of @wDN{Dumuzid} sound, @wDN{Inana}, may the churn sound! 

{9 = 9-14}
9.	The rocking of the churn will sing (?) for you, @wDN{Inana}, may it thus make you joyous! The good shepherd, the man of sweet songs, will loudly (?) sing songs for you; lady, with all the sweetest things, @wDN{Inana}, may he make your heart joyous! 

{15 = 15-20}
15.	Lady, when you enter the cattle-pen, @wDN{Inana}, 
16.	the cattle-pen will indeed rejoice over you. 
17.	Mistress, when you enter the sheepfold, @wDN{Inana}, 
18.	the sheepfold will indeed rejoice over you. 
19.	When you enter the feeding-pen, 
20.	healthy ewes will spread out their wool for you. 

{21 = 21-24}
21.	May the holy sheepfold abundantly provide (?) you with butter, 
22.	may the cattle-pen produce butter and cream for you! 
23.	May abundance endure in the sheepfold, 
24.	may the days of @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}} be numerous! 

{25 = 25-26}
25.	May my spouse, a ewe cherishing its lamb, be praised with sweet admiration! 
